decisions taken
  "twitter.comn" directive: the literal token appears in no URL or Domain of
    this export. Any URL containing it necessarily contains "twitter.com", so
    the filter was applied on that substring -- a superset of the literal
    rule -- removing 1 row (a twitter.com URL carrying Status "Illegal
    gambling" and Rank 16, which would otherwise have led the Section C
    top-ranked table). The exclusion and its count are declared in the
    report's method note rather than applied silently.
  §B1 licence number / registration jurisdiction: reported as "No disponible"
    for all 29 brands. The export carries no such column and the report is
    self-contained with no external lookups; per the spec's "nunca inventar un
    valor" rule these cells are declared unavailable instead of being filled
    with unverified data. Legal entity is filled only where the brand matches
    a §1.3 A platform, which supplies that datum.
  §B1 brand matching: a URL counts toward a brand when the brand token is a
    host label of the URL, or of its seed brand, that equals the token, begins
    with it, or carries it hyphen-delimited. Path and query text are never
    matched -- doing so pulled in unrelated sites carrying a brand inside a
    redirect parameter. Variants and redirects are attributed to their seed
    per §2 brand(fila). BETSONN matches 0 URLs and is rendered as an explicit
    empty state.
  registrable(host): eTLD+1 via a two-label public-suffix table, so subdomains
    and variants inherit their platform's IVA class (§2.1).
  narrative (§5) mentions neither VAT registration, legality nor blocking;
    the IVA classification surfaces only in Sections C and D and in the §B1
    legal-entity column.

